00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:56.993
- [Mark] All right, Lima and Larry.

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:02.150
We had Amanda's final
court hearing this morning,

00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:03.590
which is a big day.

00:01:03.590 --> 00:01:05.880
A couple of things in Amanda's future

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:08.530
were hinging on what the judge said today.

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:11.570
So fill us in on what happened, Lima?

00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:14.380
- So originally as
discussed in the last video,

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:17.920
we were going for an LPS conservatorship.

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:22.770
And the purpose was to get
Amanda committed to a program

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:25.620
and to ensure that we
had power of attorney

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:27.420
to make the decisions for Amanda,

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:30.770
since she was not capable of
making decisions for herself.

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:32.763
So she was a prime candidate.

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:36.840
These conservatorships are
extremely difficult to get

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:38.370
because there's a lot of evidence

00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:39.700
that needs to be demonstrated.

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:42.040
And Amanda had all of that checked off.

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:46.170
The issue with that was
that we were not able

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:48.890
to have communication between the jail

00:01:48.890 --> 00:01:50.350
and the doctor at the jail,

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:52.210
but we had everything else on our end

00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:55.130
with a second doctor referring it.

00:01:55.130 --> 00:01:58.130
And so Amanda has a public defender.

00:01:58.130 --> 00:02:03.130
As a public defender,
they have so many clients

00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:08.130
that it's really hard for them to dedicate

00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:09.440
the time required

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:12.890
to actually push something
like that through.

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:17.890
And so, because of the fact
that we didn't have anything

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:20.660
from the other end,
which was the jail side,

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:23.460
we weren't able to push the
conservatorship through.

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:25.510
So in the last 72 hours,

00:02:25.510 --> 00:02:27.720
I've been trying to do damage control.

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:30.400
And I actually woke up at 2:30 a.m.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:31.950
this morning to make sure that court

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:34.810
at 8:30 in the morning went fine.

00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:39.810
And we diverted to put in a court order

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:45.170
for Amanda to complete
one year of treatment.

00:02:45.170 --> 00:02:47.510
So she risks that if
she doesn't complete it,

00:02:47.510 --> 00:02:48.973
she goes back to jail.

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:53.390
- [Mark] So Amanda today,
this is the first time

00:02:53.390 --> 00:02:55.160
I've seen her in two months, I think.

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:56.810
Almost two months.

00:02:56.810 --> 00:02:58.520
This was a totally different Amanda.

00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:00.356
- Yes, this is the--
- I didn't even recognize her.

00:03:00.356 --> 00:03:01.410
- This is the Amanda,

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:05.310
I called her Amanda Bear because
she's been quite responsive

00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:09.900
and she's doing so much better
just being off the streets

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:13.560
and in an environment where
she's being controlled.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:15.770
So I told her she's
doing the hard work now.

00:03:15.770 --> 00:03:19.720
So any program that we place her in,

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:22.050
then she's gonna already have herself

00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:24.220
prepared to participate.

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:27.100
So she has come along quite well

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:30.110
with the help of Lima and Mark.

00:03:30.110 --> 00:03:33.370
It's just encouraging to
know that there's still

00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:37.150
good-hearted people that will
step up to such a big at bat.

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:39.560
I mean, this is really big.

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:41.926
- [Mark] Yeah, Lima's been amazing.

00:03:41.926 --> 00:03:43.890
- Thank you guys.
- She's detailed person.

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:47.080
I used to tell my troops,
pay attention to detail.

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:49.220
If I could have had her
picture on the example,

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:50.360
she would have been there.

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:51.690
- [Mark] I've never
interacted with somebody

00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:53.940
who's so thorough and so buttoned up

00:03:53.940 --> 00:03:55.760
about every single thing.
- Daily, daily.

00:03:55.760 --> 00:03:56.870
- [Mark] And figuring out some way

00:03:56.870 --> 00:03:57.870
to get around this loophole

00:03:57.870 --> 00:03:59.470
and figure out the
solution to that problem.

00:03:59.470 --> 00:04:02.160
And she just is, has been relentless.

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:05.100
- Exactly.
- And Amanda this morning was,

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:06.770
she was unrecognizable.
- Adorable.

00:04:06.770 --> 00:04:07.900
- [Mark] She's put on about what?

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:10.490
15, 20 pounds probably.
- She looks like her old self.

00:04:10.490 --> 00:04:12.260
- She walked into the courtroom and said,

00:04:12.260 --> 00:04:13.460
good morning, your honor.

00:04:13.460 --> 00:04:14.650
And she was respectful.

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:16.073
She didn't talk over people.

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:20.430
And the hardest part for
me to watch, this is long.

00:04:20.430 --> 00:04:23.220
She was up there 15 minutes,
at least, 20 minutes.

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:26.020
The DA was reading her
off all this legalese

00:04:26.020 --> 00:04:28.100
about how she potentially
could be going to prison

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:28.933
for three years.

00:04:28.933 --> 00:04:30.860
And the fines could be
this and all these things

00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:32.273
if she doesn't do things,

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:35.810
if she screws up with going to rehab

00:04:35.810 --> 00:04:37.233
or she escapes or whatever.

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:42.510
And she handled it
perfectly all throughout.

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:45.983
She was so respectful and so calm.

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:49.660
It was hard to watch,
but she did a great job.

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:51.643
- Incredible.
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:55.110
I do think that it's
important to note that

00:04:57.820 --> 00:05:01.180
even though all of the
documents were sent in file,

00:05:01.180 --> 00:05:03.640
or that all of the documents on my end

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:06.020
were filled out and sent
and even the program

00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:10.173
that I had Amanda accepted into,

00:05:11.940 --> 00:05:14.890
nobody at the courthouse
actually had the paperwork,

00:05:14.890 --> 00:05:16.880
even though it was emailed to them.

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:18.660
And so it's really important to note

00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:22.800
that in cases where
it's a public defender,

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:27.797
there's a lot of people,
these are very short trials.

00:05:31.192 --> 00:05:33.940
It's really easy to just
get lost in all of that.

00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:36.430
So I think that it's really important

00:05:36.430 --> 00:05:37.510
for other people out there

00:05:37.510 --> 00:05:39.340
that are looking to do something like this

00:05:39.340 --> 00:05:40.750
for their family member

00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:43.740
to not just purely lean on the system

00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:45.630
and expect that just because that person

00:05:45.630 --> 00:05:46.710
has a representative,

00:05:46.710 --> 00:05:50.920
that that representative
will do what it takes,

00:05:50.920 --> 00:05:54.080
because it's not necessarily
that they don't care.

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:56.190
It's just that they're overworked.

00:05:56.190 --> 00:05:59.950
And there's just so many people
that don't have resources.

00:05:59.950 --> 00:06:01.280
- [Mark] I think you've
done most of the hard work,

00:06:01.280 --> 00:06:03.730
in Amanda's case.
- Yeah, it's been really hard.

00:06:06.040 --> 00:06:08.070
- [Mark] The rehab that Amanda's going to,

00:06:08.070 --> 00:06:09.570
there were two options, right?

00:06:10.430 --> 00:06:13.120
- So when I pitched the
idea to the courthouse

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:15.090
of Amanda going to a program,

00:06:15.090 --> 00:06:17.140
what I did was I used the documentation

00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:19.300
from the LPS conservatorship.

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:23.120
And so one of the documents is a one-pager

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:24.750
on Amanda's history.

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:29.010
And what that is is that I
worked with Larry to compose it.

00:06:29.010 --> 00:06:33.370
And it details all of
her mental illnesses,

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:36.550
the diagnoses, her medical record,

00:06:36.550 --> 00:06:40.620
like, just a very short summary,
jail time that she has done

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:44.650
and certain issues that
she's had in the past,

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:46.090
or even traumas.

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:49.270
And so super short one-pager

00:06:49.270 --> 00:06:52.330
that shows the severity of the issue.

00:06:52.330 --> 00:06:55.920
And we took that one-pager
and we pitched the concept

00:06:55.920 --> 00:06:58.760
of being able to have
Amanda not do jail time

00:06:58.760 --> 00:07:01.380
or not just be released on the street

00:07:01.380 --> 00:07:03.866
where she's gonna end up
re-offending and in jail--

00:07:03.866 --> 00:07:06.070
- [Mark] She would have been
free for 10 days, right?

00:07:06.070 --> 00:07:07.630
- Not for 10 days.

00:07:07.630 --> 00:07:11.170
She would have been potentially released

00:07:11.170 --> 00:07:12.570
the last time I came.

00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:14.950
So that last day that I went to court,

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:18.370
she was set to be released
back onto the street

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:20.780
because there were no
other options for her.

00:07:20.780 --> 00:07:25.160
And so initially, when speaking
to the district attorney,

00:07:25.160 --> 00:07:29.160
I notified her that this
was not Amanda's first time,

00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:31.650
which was already
something that was known,

00:07:31.650 --> 00:07:36.360
and that she's in a very bad mental state.

00:07:36.360 --> 00:07:39.010
And so that was documented
on the one-page document,

00:07:39.010 --> 00:07:41.200
because if you have
anything more than one page,

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:43.140
they don't have time to look at it.

00:07:43.140 --> 00:07:46.370
And so based on that information

00:07:46.370 --> 00:07:49.100
is what made them shift gears

00:07:49.100 --> 00:07:51.670
and say that if we were
willing to take responsibility,

00:07:51.670 --> 00:07:53.520
so basically myself,

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:57.380
willing to ensure that I report
everything to the courthouse

00:07:57.380 --> 00:08:00.090
and make sure that Amanda
doesn't violate anything

00:08:00.090 --> 00:08:04.550
and ensure that she follows court order,

00:08:04.550 --> 00:08:09.550
that they would consider giving
her a mandated one-year plan

00:08:09.930 --> 00:08:14.930
which would be the essential
path of an LPS conservatorship.

00:08:16.064 --> 00:08:17.360
- [Mark] And she understood
it completely in court.

00:08:17.360 --> 00:08:20.360
And she agreed to at all
with no one's coaxing.

00:08:20.360 --> 00:08:22.230
She just said, yes, this is what I want.

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:23.410
- Yeah, and this is something

00:08:23.410 --> 00:08:25.950
that Larry has been talking
to her for a while about.

00:08:25.950 --> 00:08:29.360
So they talk daily and
I've been really surprised

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:32.400
that she's been actually
very excited about treatment

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:37.400
because I have to be careful
with what I say specifically

00:08:38.300 --> 00:08:39.300
due to HIPAA law.

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:40.810
And I can't state anything

00:08:40.810 --> 00:08:43.170
that is not already publicly known,

00:08:43.170 --> 00:08:48.050
but one of the things that
we have been questioning

00:08:48.050 --> 00:08:53.050
is Amanda's current diagnoses
from medical professionals.

00:08:53.980 --> 00:08:58.290
And the reason for that
is because all of her,

00:08:58.290 --> 00:09:01.700
the past seven facilities that she went to

00:09:01.700 --> 00:09:03.570
were very short stays

00:09:03.570 --> 00:09:07.713
and she was actually diagnosed
while using, exactly.

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:14.507
So it wasn't something that
we can really go off of.

00:09:14.507 --> 00:09:16.540
And so now that she's been clean in jail

00:09:16.540 --> 00:09:18.430
for the last two months,

00:09:18.430 --> 00:09:22.100
we actually could have
had her transferred today,

00:09:22.100 --> 00:09:25.360
but we chose to hold her
bed until October 10th

00:09:25.360 --> 00:09:29.080
so that she knows for a fact
that this is not a right.

00:09:29.080 --> 00:09:30.610
This is a privilege.

00:09:30.610 --> 00:09:33.510
And that there are consequences,
that if she messes up,

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:34.760
she will go back to jail.

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:37.200
So we really want her to understand

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:39.530
that this is an opportunity for her

00:09:39.530 --> 00:09:41.610
and she needs to take
full advantage of it.

00:09:41.610 --> 00:09:43.780
And even though she's
saying that she's excited

00:09:43.780 --> 00:09:46.700
for treatment right now and
that she really wants it,

00:09:46.700 --> 00:09:50.880
we want her to be really
hungry for it when she gets it.

00:09:50.880 --> 00:09:53.480
Because as you know, it's very expensive

00:09:53.480 --> 00:09:57.300
and we've pulled a lot of
strings to make this happen.

00:09:57.300 --> 00:09:59.370
The options from the courthouse,

00:09:59.370 --> 00:10:01.720
when we pitched them the concept of Amanda

00:10:01.720 --> 00:10:06.070
going to mental health care
for a year instead of jail

00:10:06.070 --> 00:10:09.020
or instead of being released
and just being homeless again,

00:10:10.290 --> 00:10:12.530
they have a court diversion program.

00:10:12.530 --> 00:10:17.530
Those diversion programs can
have 100, up to 200 patients,

00:10:18.580 --> 00:10:22.260
and you're not getting one-on-one therapy

00:10:22.260 --> 00:10:24.910
and you're not getting the
necessary care that you need.

00:10:24.910 --> 00:10:27.320
The program that Amanda
is gonna be going to

00:10:27.320 --> 00:10:29.650
has seven patients, seven beds,

00:10:29.650 --> 00:10:33.090
and it's intensive therapy
throughout the day.

00:10:33.090 --> 00:10:35.380
And there's a lot of different activities

00:10:35.380 --> 00:10:37.500
and they integrate
family therapy in there.

00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:41.800
So then Larry will be
able to work with Amanda

00:10:41.800 --> 00:10:44.833
- [Mark] And this kind
of care is expensive?

00:10:45.833 --> 00:10:48.069
- Yes, yes.
- You don't have rehab

00:10:48.069 --> 00:10:52.910
for seven patients for $1,000 a week.

00:10:52.910 --> 00:10:56.390
It's expensive.
- Yeah, so before I continue,

00:10:56.390 --> 00:10:58.640
I would like to state
that I am not a doctor.

00:10:58.640 --> 00:10:59.690
I am not a lawyer.

00:10:59.690 --> 00:11:01.940
So my advice should not be taken

00:11:01.940 --> 00:11:04.860
in replacement for
medical or legal advice.

00:11:04.860 --> 00:11:08.040
I'm just trying to share
information with people

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:10.170
because this is a lot of information

00:11:10.170 --> 00:11:14.130
that has taken so many years to build up.

00:11:14.130 --> 00:11:18.190
And it's just a lot more simple

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:20.070
when you actually know what to search for.

00:11:20.070 --> 00:11:25.070
So the other factor is
that, can I talk about the,

00:11:27.360 --> 00:11:30.410
I know you told me not
to mention the comments.

00:11:30.410 --> 00:11:31.243
- [Mark] Oh, go ahead.

00:11:31.243 --> 00:11:33.071
I mean, there's been
lots of negative comments

00:11:33.071 --> 00:11:34.668
that don't understand what you're doing

00:11:34.668 --> 00:11:36.835
or what you're offering
or what you're all about.

00:11:36.835 --> 00:11:37.910
So if you wanna clarify that, please do.

00:11:37.910 --> 00:11:38.743
- Exactly.

00:11:38.743 --> 00:11:43.480
So I am the founder and
CEO of a tech startup

00:11:43.480 --> 00:11:46.320
and we build technology software

00:11:46.320 --> 00:11:49.330
for healthcare providers, mental health.

00:11:49.330 --> 00:11:53.340
And the treatment centers
that we are sending Amanda to

00:11:53.340 --> 00:11:57.630
are not owned by me and I
do not get paid by them.

00:11:57.630 --> 00:12:01.280
So it's really important
to clarify that when,

00:12:01.280 --> 00:12:03.990
in the past, when I've
said that the technology

00:12:03.990 --> 00:12:07.810
that I provide facilities
to is evidence-based,

00:12:07.810 --> 00:12:10.400
that means that it's
already been validated

00:12:10.400 --> 00:12:11.910
and proven to work.

00:12:11.910 --> 00:12:15.160
So we're not using anybody as a guinea pig

00:12:15.160 --> 00:12:18.230
and we're not testing anything on anybody.

00:12:18.230 --> 00:12:20.660
When I say that we're
providing the technology

00:12:20.660 --> 00:12:23.890
to treatment centers
for research purposes,

00:12:23.890 --> 00:12:26.980
those research purposes
are to demonstrate a value

00:12:26.980 --> 00:12:28.310
to a treatment center.

00:12:28.310 --> 00:12:30.330
So they're already making money

00:12:30.330 --> 00:12:31.770
and they're already getting paid.

00:12:31.770 --> 00:12:33.120
- [Mark] These are various, I mean,

00:12:33.120 --> 00:12:37.060
the list of rehab facilities
that AURA works with

00:12:37.060 --> 00:12:37.910
is an impressive list.

00:12:37.910 --> 00:12:39.130
And you've already been working
with them long before you--

00:12:39.130 --> 00:12:41.700
- So they're very
prestigious facilities that,

00:12:41.700 --> 00:12:44.730
like I said, most people cannot get into.

00:12:44.730 --> 00:12:47.350
And I personally cannot
afford those facilities

00:12:47.350 --> 00:12:48.340
for my sisters.

00:12:48.340 --> 00:12:52.480
And my sisters would be
Amanda price's times two.

00:12:52.480 --> 00:12:57.480
So my initial initiative
for wanting to help Amanda

00:12:58.610 --> 00:13:00.580
or wanting to objectively help someone

00:13:00.580 --> 00:13:05.580
that I'm not related to,
that is basically to prove,

00:13:05.620 --> 00:13:09.710
so what I'm trying to prove
here is not my technology

00:13:09.710 --> 00:13:11.343
or it's not my,

00:13:13.120 --> 00:13:17.010
it's initially that we
need long-term treatment

00:13:17.010 --> 00:13:19.790
and we need additional
tools for therapists

00:13:19.790 --> 00:13:22.444
so that they can measure
how patients are feeling.

00:13:22.444 --> 00:13:23.395
- [Mark] And your company provides

00:13:23.395 --> 00:13:25.394
those additional tools for therapists.

00:13:25.394 --> 00:13:26.280
That's all.
- Exactly.

00:13:26.280 --> 00:13:27.910
And so the facilities--

00:13:27.910 --> 00:13:28.930
- [Mark] People had you, like,

00:13:28.930 --> 00:13:30.380
I think you were performing lobotomies--

00:13:30.380 --> 00:13:32.170
- No, not at all.

00:13:32.170 --> 00:13:35.140
And the facilities that
ironically I work with

00:13:35.140 --> 00:13:37.243
and that I supply this technology to,

00:13:38.310 --> 00:13:40.530
I can't afford to send my sisters to.

00:13:40.530 --> 00:13:44.040
So the goal is to really
make this scalable

00:13:44.040 --> 00:13:46.590
and get access to it through insurance.

00:13:46.590 --> 00:13:47.737
- [Mark] And it'll help
the world understand

00:13:47.737 --> 00:13:49.360
how to treat these patients better.

00:13:49.360 --> 00:13:50.620
- Exactly.

00:13:50.620 --> 00:13:54.040
And then the last factor is
that I really do want to clarify

00:13:54.040 --> 00:13:58.130
that all of the funds go to giving.org.

00:13:58.130 --> 00:14:03.130
So I highly recommend people
to look into what Giving is

00:14:04.090 --> 00:14:06.850
and who they are and who they represent,

00:14:06.850 --> 00:14:08.580
because they've also represented

00:14:08.580 --> 00:14:13.580
several high-profile charities
like Miley Cyrus's charity.

00:14:17.280 --> 00:14:19.120
I can't remember the name of it.

00:14:19.120 --> 00:14:22.060
But there's been several,

00:14:22.060 --> 00:14:24.600
people should do the
research on who Giving is.

00:14:24.600 --> 00:14:26.740
There's been a lot of
assumptions on who I am

00:14:26.740 --> 00:14:28.480
and the fact that I'm not a real person

00:14:28.480 --> 00:14:33.160
because my company was registered
under another last name.

00:14:33.160 --> 00:14:34.560
That was my old last name.

00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:36.470
I did get married recently.

00:14:36.470 --> 00:14:38.820
So I am a real person

00:14:38.820 --> 00:14:42.480
and a lot of speculation from people

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:43.313
that are not my clients

00:14:43.313 --> 00:14:46.660
- [Mark] I mean, again,
YouTube just comments.

00:14:46.660 --> 00:14:50.500
A lot of people just like
to create a controversy.

00:14:50.500 --> 00:14:55.190
So, Larry, what's your
impression of what Lima has done?

00:14:55.190 --> 00:14:57.110
- Lima has been tremendous.

00:14:57.110 --> 00:15:00.490
She's been such a light in my life

00:15:00.490 --> 00:15:03.600
because I was dealing with
Amanda all those months.

00:15:03.600 --> 00:15:05.850
And I found out, in retrospect,

00:15:05.850 --> 00:15:07.780
I didn't really know what I was doing,

00:15:07.780 --> 00:15:09.640
but I had to do something.

00:15:09.640 --> 00:15:12.860
So what Lima has done is brought to me

00:15:12.860 --> 00:15:16.120
an organized plan for Amanda.

00:15:16.120 --> 00:15:17.810
And that's what I never had.

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:19.080
I never had anybody say,

00:15:19.080 --> 00:15:21.862
well, what are we gonna
do after we do this?

00:15:21.862 --> 00:15:25.910
A conservatorship was
difficult, but there was a plan.

00:15:25.910 --> 00:15:27.130
And she shared it with me.

00:15:27.130 --> 00:15:28.390
And that's where we are now.

00:15:28.390 --> 00:15:31.680
We're in the process of implementing it.

00:15:31.680 --> 00:15:33.510
And her presence and her attention

00:15:33.510 --> 00:15:36.380
to taking care of all of the things

00:15:36.380 --> 00:15:39.210
that people don't pay attention
to has made a difference,

00:15:39.210 --> 00:15:40.230
even today.
- She's been involved

00:15:40.230 --> 00:15:41.640
in Amanda's life for how long?

00:15:41.640 --> 00:15:42.793
Roughly a month or so?

00:15:44.250 --> 00:15:48.020
There's been so much
progress in that last month.

00:15:48.020 --> 00:15:49.840
More than in the last five years, right?

00:15:49.840 --> 00:15:50.673
- Exactly.

00:15:50.673 --> 00:15:53.500
And so when she said that
she's gonna help my family,

00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:57.410
not just for now but
for some time to come,

00:15:57.410 --> 00:15:58.900
that means everything to me.

00:15:58.900 --> 00:16:00.610
- [Mark] Well, just seeing
who Amanda was today

00:16:00.610 --> 00:16:03.435
this morning in court was--
- Incredible.

00:16:03.435 --> 00:16:04.683
- [Mark] I couldn't, I
didn't even recognize her.

00:16:04.683 --> 00:16:06.770
- Yes, she looked very good.

00:16:06.770 --> 00:16:07.677
- [Mark] Is that the old
Amanda that you knew?

00:16:07.677 --> 00:16:09.490
- That's Amanda Bear.

00:16:09.490 --> 00:16:10.323
That's her.

00:16:11.710 --> 00:16:14.940
- It's also pretty interesting
that Larry is a veteran

00:16:14.940 --> 00:16:17.810
and his insurance is covered by the VA.

00:16:17.810 --> 00:16:21.820
And Amanda actually should
be covered by the VA

00:16:21.820 --> 00:16:24.250
and half of the costs
that we're trying to raise

00:16:24.250 --> 00:16:26.290
on GoFundMe for her right now

00:16:26.290 --> 00:16:29.870
should actually be completely
covered under insurance,

00:16:29.870 --> 00:16:31.730
but due to loopholes

00:16:31.730 --> 00:16:34.910
and certain things that
Larry was unaware of

00:16:34.910 --> 00:16:39.670
to file for his daughter,
it's run its course.

00:16:39.670 --> 00:16:44.520
And for example, there's TRICARE,

00:16:45.870 --> 00:16:47.930
which I'm still trying to figure out

00:16:47.930 --> 00:16:49.830
because for some reason
they're not covering Larry

00:16:49.830 --> 00:16:51.610
but we're unsure of why.

00:16:51.610 --> 00:16:55.040
And then the second option is CHAMPVA.

00:16:55.040 --> 00:16:58.210
And so Amanda is completely dependent

00:16:58.210 --> 00:16:59.990
on Larry for everything.

00:16:59.990 --> 00:17:03.450
And before your child turns 18,

00:17:03.450 --> 00:17:06.543
which this was happening to
Amanda before she was 18,

00:17:08.240 --> 00:17:09.740
there's something that you can file

00:17:09.740 --> 00:17:11.563
which is helpless child status.

00:17:13.722 --> 00:17:17.070
And had Larry filed it,

00:17:17.070 --> 00:17:19.630
we would have no problem
covering Amanda's care.

00:17:19.630 --> 00:17:24.630
So because of that, it's been
extremely challenging for him

00:17:25.240 --> 00:17:27.090
to provide any type of support

00:17:27.090 --> 00:17:29.170
even though he did serve his country.

00:17:29.170 --> 00:17:34.170
He's 60% disabled from his
service, and he's not able to,

00:17:34.590 --> 00:17:37.460
he has to watch his daughter struggle

00:17:37.460 --> 00:17:40.250
and die in front of him
without being able to cover

00:17:40.250 --> 00:17:42.353
her treatment costs.

00:17:42.353 --> 00:17:47.340
And navigating the VA is
a totally different thing.

00:17:47.340 --> 00:17:48.730
But if you are a veteran

00:17:48.730 --> 00:17:51.440
and your child has mental health issues,

00:17:51.440 --> 00:17:55.430
I highly recommend that
before they turn 18

00:17:55.430 --> 00:17:58.013
to ask about helpless child status.

00:17:58.850 --> 00:18:00.720
- [Mark] Larry, tell me
about Amanda's childhood.

00:18:00.720 --> 00:18:03.320
So tell me about Amanda's mother.

00:18:03.320 --> 00:18:06.310
- Amanda, her mother's a beautician.

00:18:06.310 --> 00:18:11.310
She's very busy and
successful at what she does.

00:18:11.480 --> 00:18:13.700
So when I met her, I
was just a workaholic.

00:18:13.700 --> 00:18:15.617
So it was a lot of fun times.

00:18:15.617 --> 00:18:17.520
We got along very well.

00:18:17.520 --> 00:18:20.520
Matter of fact, we met at an NBC sitcom.

00:18:20.520 --> 00:18:24.950
We were just out in Burbank
going in to see a TV show.

00:18:24.950 --> 00:18:27.160
So after that, we got along well,

00:18:27.160 --> 00:18:31.520
and as a result, Amanda was born.

00:18:31.520 --> 00:18:34.200
But even during our courtship,

00:18:34.200 --> 00:18:36.340
I didn't get along with her

00:18:36.340 --> 00:18:38.430
because she had a different personality,

00:18:38.430 --> 00:18:40.100
like Jekyll and Hyde.

00:18:40.100 --> 00:18:42.500
So I dealt with that
before Amanda was born.

00:18:42.500 --> 00:18:43.890
But after Amanda was born,

00:18:43.890 --> 00:18:46.310
I saw how it was affecting Amanda.

00:18:46.310 --> 00:18:49.210
So I decided Amanda was
only about 10 or 11 months.

00:18:49.210 --> 00:18:50.700
I said, I gotta make a change.

00:18:50.700 --> 00:18:52.710
I gotta do something different.

00:18:52.710 --> 00:18:57.560
And I just went and talked to
someone about going to court.

00:18:57.560 --> 00:19:01.500
So I took custody of
Amanda at three years old.

00:19:01.500 --> 00:19:05.000
So since then, I just raised Amanda.

00:19:05.000 --> 00:19:10.000
I did my retail business
and raised Amanda until now.

00:19:10.494 --> 00:19:12.090
- [Mark] And Amanda's mom was in her life?

00:19:12.090 --> 00:19:13.840
- She was not in her life.

00:19:13.840 --> 00:19:17.350
After we got the legal
custody and control,

00:19:17.350 --> 00:19:19.520
she just disappeared.

00:19:19.520 --> 00:19:22.180
So Amanda and I just
moved on with our lives

00:19:22.180 --> 00:19:24.660
from elementary school on through

00:19:24.660 --> 00:19:27.140
the University of Northridge.

00:19:27.140 --> 00:19:28.930
We just had a good life.

00:19:28.930 --> 00:19:31.550
I relived my life through her childhood.

00:19:31.550 --> 00:19:34.300
So I must say, I know
Amanda had a lot of fun

00:19:34.300 --> 00:19:36.710
'cause I did everything
that I could possibly do

00:19:36.710 --> 00:19:39.490
when I wasn't at the store
trying to make a living.

00:19:39.490 --> 00:19:42.030
So I told Amanda, I said,

00:19:42.030 --> 00:19:43.410
I know people say you're spoiled.

00:19:43.410 --> 00:19:46.520
I said, but we have to do
things to balance our lives.

00:19:46.520 --> 00:19:49.560
I'm always working and
we have to do those.

00:19:49.560 --> 00:19:50.700
So that's what we did.

00:19:50.700 --> 00:19:54.550
Every year we went to all the places,

00:19:54.550 --> 00:19:58.260
Knott's Berry, Disney
Land, the county fair.

00:19:58.260 --> 00:19:59.810
That was the most interesting thing,

00:19:59.810 --> 00:20:03.610
to turn her on to animals,
because city girls,

00:20:03.610 --> 00:20:06.720
they know animals but to
see them and touch them

00:20:06.720 --> 00:20:09.840
and maybe ride on, that was
the biggest thrill of her life.

00:20:09.840 --> 00:20:12.300
So I'm sure if she would remember,

00:20:12.300 --> 00:20:14.890
she would remember Knott's Berry.

00:20:14.890 --> 00:20:17.990
So I just say to you,
Amanda enjoyed her life.

00:20:17.990 --> 00:20:19.710
I spoiled her as a single parent.

00:20:19.710 --> 00:20:22.690
As a retail guy, she
was always at the mall.

00:20:22.690 --> 00:20:24.310
She was always getting stuff.

00:20:24.310 --> 00:20:26.360
I mean, that's what I did.

00:20:26.360 --> 00:20:27.363
That's my living.

00:20:28.210 --> 00:20:31.130
- So she had a good childhood?
- She had a great childhood.

00:20:31.130 --> 00:20:31.963
- [Mark] Excellent.

00:20:31.963 --> 00:20:33.890
Well, today was a great day.

00:20:33.890 --> 00:20:36.530
Amanda's got, her birthday is Sunday.

00:20:36.530 --> 00:20:38.870
She's got about 10 or 15 days

00:20:38.870 --> 00:20:43.770
before she gets taken from jail to rehab

00:20:43.770 --> 00:20:45.223
for one year exactly, right?

00:20:46.120 --> 00:20:47.580
- Yes.

00:20:47.580 --> 00:20:49.743
Thank God Miss Lima.
- Thank you.

00:20:50.850 --> 00:20:52.850
I have a little bit more

00:20:52.850 --> 00:20:54.332
and you can edit out

00:20:54.332 --> 00:20:55.165
whatever you don't wanna say.
- Let's hear it,

00:20:55.165 --> 00:20:57.410
let's hear it, let's hear it.
- Okay.

00:20:57.410 --> 00:21:00.620
First and foremost is that I spend about,

00:21:00.620 --> 00:21:03.230
like five hours a day on the phone

00:21:03.230 --> 00:21:05.400
trying to coordinate this stuff.

00:21:05.400 --> 00:21:07.630
And I don't charge for my time.

00:21:07.630 --> 00:21:10.390
And this is very
personally important to me

00:21:10.390 --> 00:21:12.000
because I do believe

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:14.810
that it will help my
sisters in the long run,

00:21:14.810 --> 00:21:18.480
but I've received a tremendous
amount of death threats.

00:21:18.480 --> 00:21:21.843
Sorry, we're gonna have to retake this.

00:21:25.576 --> 00:21:26.620
- [Mark] There's lots of death threats.

00:21:26.620 --> 00:21:28.020
I get them too, and a lot of my--

00:21:28.020 --> 00:21:31.340
- Yeah, but it's not, it's like.

00:21:31.340 --> 00:21:32.820
- [Mark] Social media is
just this cancerous thing.

00:21:32.820 --> 00:21:34.100
- Not even that.

00:21:34.100 --> 00:21:36.810
I've had people look up my,

00:21:36.810 --> 00:21:41.810
like try to find my address
and share my address.

00:21:43.500 --> 00:21:45.250
I'm not crying on camera right now.

00:21:46.750 --> 00:21:51.160
So it's like, if I was by myself,

00:21:51.160 --> 00:21:55.040
if I didn't have a
family, I'll deal with it.

00:21:55.040 --> 00:21:56.323
But the fact that like,

00:21:57.320 --> 00:21:59.520
the GoFundMe campaign has not been doing,

00:21:59.520 --> 00:22:00.850
it's been doing really amazing

00:22:00.850 --> 00:22:04.920
in terms of we have 200 donors
that are super supportive,

00:22:04.920 --> 00:22:08.760
but my husband and I
actually paid for Amanda's

00:22:08.760 --> 00:22:10.480
first month of treatment

00:22:10.480 --> 00:22:14.060
and we secured and we had to pay in cash.

00:22:14.060 --> 00:22:16.150
So we took out a line of credit

00:22:16.150 --> 00:22:17.620
and we tried to secure

00:22:17.620 --> 00:22:20.440
at least the first two months for Amanda.

00:22:20.440 --> 00:22:24.220
And it's not like we just
have money to blow around.

00:22:24.220 --> 00:22:27.800
And I also have two sick sisters
that I'm responsible for.

00:22:27.800 --> 00:22:32.010
And so for people to go, and as a startup,

00:22:32.010 --> 00:22:34.950
anybody can can start a
business, a small business.

00:22:34.950 --> 00:22:37.650
And so I don't get paid.

00:22:37.650 --> 00:22:40.700
My team, I raised a small amount of money

00:22:40.700 --> 00:22:41.720
